92
00:05:52.273 --> 00:05:58.053
♪ External reuse is not a one-time investment. ♪

93
00:05:58.967 --> 00:06:00.477
(narrator) Verse 4, case 3, left-pad.

94
00:06:00.477 --> 00:06:06.925
(narrator) Left-pad's eleven lines of JavaScript, and what they are for: three numbers, 7, 42, and 317, padded to width 3.

95
00:06:06.925 --> 00:06:12.154
(narrator) Padding bricks drop in on the left of the short ones until all three line up on the right.

96
00:06:12.154 --> 00:06:13.490
(narrator) Why: a build of bricks.

97
00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:20.287
(narrator) Your app stands on react and babel-core; babel-core stands on more packages, which stand on one tiny brick, left-pad.

98
00:06:20.287 --> 00:06:23.307
(narrator) The path down to it lights: a transitive dependency.

99
00:06:23.307 --> 00:06:38.586
(narrator) The tiny brick strains under the load, then vanishes in a puff of dust, unpublished in March 2016; the bricks above it hang in the air for a cartoon moment, then drop and tilt, and your app teeters; three builds print npm error 404, and your app gets a red cross.

100
00:06:38.586 --> 00:06:42.594
(narrator) You only listed react and babel-core; left-pad sat three levels down.

101
00:06:42.594 --> 00:06:47.997
(narrator) Next, eslint-scope 3.7.2, its maintainer's account taken over, and an npm token sliding away.

102
00:06:47.997 --> 00:07:02.462
(narrator) The principle bricks follow in turn: avoid reusing trivial code, beside a one-line isArray; strive for fewer package dependencies, as a shelf of eight package bricks loses its five trivial ones and tags say each can break, be hijacked, or disappear.

103
00:07:02.462 --> 00:07:08.561
(narrator) A homemade encrypt function is crossed out for a vetted crypto library brick: don't roll your own crypto.

104
00:07:08.561 --> 00:07:20.703
(narrator) Last, a well-maintained profile card is ticked over an abandoned one, and at a brick wall with a gap, the popular brick is too wide to fit while a smaller brick fills the gap: fit matters more than popularity.

105
00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:22.680
♪ Left-pad: eleven lines ♪

106
00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.820
♪ That pad a string on the left. ♪

107
00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:26.780
♪ Babel and React pulled it in ♪

108
00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.460
